            <identifier label="RISM">530002116</identifier>
            <physDesc>
              <extent>18 parts</extent>
              <titlePage label="[wrapper]">
                <p>Sub tuum in F | a 4|t Voci | 2.|e Violini | con | Organo e Violone | Auth. di Greg. Werner.</p>
              </titlePage>
              <handList>
                <hand xmlns:xl="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" medium="brown ink" type="main">Gregor Joseph Werner</hand>
                <hand xmlns:xl="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" medium="brown ink" type="main">Copyist Esterh&#xE1;zy 1</hand>
                <hand xmlns:xl="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" medium="brown ink" type="main">unidentified</hand>
              </handList>
              <physMedium>
                <p>three sets of parts:<lb/>(1) 7 parts: partly autograph manuscript, ca. 1740, 22 x 17 cm, hand-ruled paper, 7 staves (11 mm)<lb/>(2) 1 part: manuscript copy, ca. 1750, 22 x 17 cm, hand-ruled paper, 7 staves (11 mm)<lb/>(3) 10 parts: manuscript copy, ca. 1790, 15 x 22 cm, hand-ruled paper, 5 staves (10 mm)</p>
              </physMedium>
            </physDesc>
            <physLoc>
              <repository>
                <corpName role=""/>
                <geogName role=""/>
                <identifier auth="RISM" auth.uri="http://www.rism.info">H-Bn</identifier>
                <ptr target="https://copia.oszk.hu/kotta/subtuum-in-f/" mimetype="" label="digitized version"/>
                <ptr target="https://nektar.oszk.hu/hu/manifestation/2706571" mimetype="" label="catalogue entry"/>
              </repository>
              <identifier>Ms.mus III.240</identifier>
            </physLoc>
            <notesStmt>
              <annot type="source_description">
                <p>first set of parts: S coro (2), T coro (2), B coro (2), vla 1 (1), vla 2 (1), vlne (1), org (1); second set: A coro (2); third set: S coro (3x; 3, 3, 2), A coro (2x; 3, 2), T coro (3), B coro (3), vla 1 (3), vla 2 (3), vlne (2)</p>
                <p>first set of parts by Werner and Copyist Esterh&#xE1;zy 1, although the division is not particularly clear; S, vlne, and org are likely by Werner, as well as the clefs in the first staff of each part</p>
                <p>wrapper originally belonged to WerW I.5.16, as evident from original inventory numbers</p>
              </annot>
              <annot type="links">
                <ptr mimetype=""/>
              </annot>
            </notesStmt>
